% pass inside the 20) \u2014 <strong>Tre Tucker</strong>'s TD equity over a goal-line back.</p><p>In the red zone MIA throw it (55% pass inside the 20) \u2014 <strong>Jalen Tolbert</strong>'s TD equity over a goal-line back.</p><h3>Game Script, Pace & Environment</h3><p><strong>Indoors</strong> \u2014 a dome removes weather variance and historically nudges passing efficiency up; a small tailwind for the passing games.</p><h3>LV \u2014 a <em>balanced</em> offense</h3><p>LV are a balanced offense \u2014 their run/pass split by game state tracks the league closely (46% pass when leading vs 44% average), so their players' usage is driven more by role than by any strong situational lean.</p><p><strong>Ashton Jeanty</strong> (18 carries, 67 yards) projects to his baseline workload \u2014 no strong script push either way in a close game.</p><p><strong>Tre Tucker</strong> projects for <strong>6 targets and 46 yards</strong>, in line with his established role in a script that neither inflates nor suppresses the pass.</p><p>Underneath, <strong>Brock Bowers</strong> (TE, 6 targets, 49 yards) is the dependable secondary read \u2014 and note the red zone stays TE-friendly regardless of score, so his touchdown equity holds up even if the game script shifts.</p><h3>MIA \u2014 a <em>run-heavy</em> offense</h3><p>MIA are one of the league's more run-committed offenses: on early downs while <strong>leading</strong>, they pass just <strong>40%</strong> of the time, against a league average of 44% \u2014 a genuine clock-bleeding identity, not noise (it holds after shrinking their sample toward the league).</p><p><strong>De'Von Achane</strong> (16 carries, 88 yards) projects to his baseline workload \u2014 no strong script push either way in a close game.</p><p><strong>Jalen Tolbert</strong> projects for <strong>4 targets and 27 yards</strong>, in line with his established role in a script that neither inflates nor suppresses the pass.</p><p>Underneath, <strong>Greg Dulcich</strong> (TE, 4 targets, 33 yards) is the dependable secondary read \u2014 and note the red zone stays TE-friendly regardless of score, so his touchdown equity holds up even if the game script shifts.</p><h3>What to watch</h3><p>The single biggest swing factor is <strong>availability</strong> \u2014 use the injury tool in the sidebar to mark anyone out; a starter's absence doesn't just remove his line, it <em>redistributes</em> his targets and carries to specific teammates, and the report and projections rebuild around it. Beyond that: if this game breaks toward the projected 3-point margin, the <strong>garbage-time backups</strong> (the \u25c6-flagged rows below) are where soft lines and real edge tend to appear \u2014 those depth players get fed in blowouts, and the market is slowest to price them.</p><p><em>This preview and the projections below regenerate through the week as injuries, weather and line moves update the inputs.</em></p></div>","teams":[{"team":"MIA","col":"#2CD3C6","players":[{"name":"Malik Willis","pos":"QB","starter":true,"minor":false,"markets":[{"label":"Pass yards","proj":175.22,"book":183.5,"over_th":123.15,"under_th":187.81,"over_am":"\u2212115","under_am":"\u2212114","pover":46,"call":"none","ev":2.1,"edge":-8.3,"skew":false},{"label":"Pass TDs","proj":0.91,"book":0.5,"over_th":0.0,"under_th":0.37,"over_am":"\u2212221","under_am":"+166","pover":43,"call":"UNDER","ev":51.4,"edge":0.4,"skew":true}],"td":{"pct":22.1,"fair":"4/1","book":"3/1","value":false},"d":{"pass_yards":{"m":175.22,"q":[0.0,0.08,153.92,323.35,521.98],"line":183.5,"od":1.87,"ud":1.88},"pass_td":{"m":0.91,"q":[0.0,0.0,0.0,1.84,4.38],"line":0.5,"od":1.45,"ud":2.67},"rush_yards":{"m":18.45,"q":[0.0,1.31,13.54,30.87,50.24],"line":39.5,"od":1.88,"ud":1.88},"rush_att":{"m":3.45,"q":[0.0,1.06,3.13,5.2,8.31],"line":7.5,"od":1.99,"ud":1.79}}},{"name":"De'Von Achane","pos":"RB","starter":true,"minor":false,"markets":[{"label":"Rush yards","proj":88.19,"book":69.5,"over_th":71.11,"under_th":87.3